  "source": [
    {
      "kind": "client",
      "evidence": "Global.Text 4229 'Snowy Canyon' (title), 77961 (card), objective 76355; icon 678."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "data/content/dungeons/snowy_canyon.json: difficulty 5, zone 'Snowhill', enemies ['Unga Frostclaw', 'Ice Crawlers', 'Ice Trolls', 'Icetroll Champion', 'Yetis', 'Yeti Pounders', 'Elusive Tranquil Sasquatch', 'Unga Frostclaw']."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Door at [421.33, 84.55, 643.13]: BJX fork Battles.lua:10 (Npcs.json Id 46189, sh_gates_01.adr). (R) the fork's own placement, not a captured one. Region Snowhill, place Snowhill."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 32 ('Snowy Canyon (the live dungeon: ice trolls and yetis fighting over the canyon from the west end, Unga Frostcla'): scene sh_canyon_combat, entry, exit, 7 waves, 27 spawns ({'Ice Troll': 9, 'Yeti Sentry': 9, 'Yeti': 8, 'Unga Frostclaw': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1231 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sh_canyon_combat has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 75 coins / 260 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier. Door actor 100000046189: reference Npcs.json Id 46189, model 111, name 4229, at [421.33, 84.55, 643.13]."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) The guide's main goal is the one goal shown from the start and is done with the fork's last goal; the steps before it stay, as the triggers of its waves and boss."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Guide overlay by scripts/dungeon_fights.py from data/content/dungeons/snowy_canyon.json."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0136 (2026-11-11): the Yetis that fight wear model 51 sasquatch_01.adr, the yeti body the fork's wave Yeti 46010 wears; 4547 sh_standard_yeti_01.adr is a banner with no skeleton, the Frosty Yeti starter's look."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "rc-0137 prize wheel: fandom 'Snowy Canyon' (revision 49151) lists one prize wheel per combat job and a 117-coin slot; any other job spins the items every job's wheel holds. Archer: the wiki's 'Pinhole Archer Shades' is 'Pin Hole Archer Shades' in our record dungeons/snowy_canyon.json."
    }
  ]
